thub.com/users/Cre8or/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cre8or/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T18:07:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T18:07:12Z","body":"+1 on adding `remove_bone` or an equivalent function.\n\nI'm working on a glTF importer script and need a way to remove driver/control bones during import (leaving only the deformation bones), to reduce clutter. Using a separate bone collection with driver/control bones is a standard animation workflow in Blender (used for inverse kinematics, or to animate meta-parameters using driver bones), and not being able to get rid of said bones after export means my resulting Skeleton3D ends up with twice as many bones, which Godot needs to keep track of - which is wasteful.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5937496984/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]